};
```

Implementation: load steps with skill (existing include) AND course (with resources → progress where userId, prerequisites). Fetch user resources for this path's courses in one query: userProgress where userId and resource.courseId in courseIds.

Course status: completed if any linked resource COMPLETED; in-progress if any percent>0 or IN_PROGRESS; else AVAILABLE.

completedSteps = completed skills + completed courses. totalSteps = all steps (excluding? include all; alternatives count as steps but ideally "choose one" — for MVP count everything).

nextTask: first IN_PROGRESS then first AVAILABLE across the ordered steps (courses and skills interleaved by order). href: skill → /skills/{slug} (quiz exists there) or /quiz/{slug}; course → /courses/{slug}.

Dashboard: update to use nextTask.href. Let me write the code.

Then the path page renders both step kinds. Then the shell app. Lots of code — let me move fast.

